<databasescript>
<code event='postopen'><lotusscript>Sub Postopen(Source As Notesuidatabase)
	' Set the last-opened profile stamp used by the aging report header
	Dim s As New NotesSession
	Dim prof As NotesDocument
	Set prof = Source.Database.GetProfileDocument("Profile")
	If Not prof Is Nothing Then
		Call prof.ReplaceItemValue("LastOpened", Now)
		Call prof.Save(True, False)
	End If
End Sub</lotusscript></code>
</databasescript>
<launchsettings>
<noteslaunch whenopened='openframeset' frameset='fsMain'/>
<weblaunch whenopened='openxpage' xpage='HeraldryHome.xsp'/>
</launchsettings>
<!--
  HAAS - Heraldry Automation System (heraldry.nsf)
  ===========================================================================
  SYNTHETIC design export. This is a stand-in modelled on the public URL shape
  of the real Army Heraldry Automation System (heraldryhome.nsf/*.xsp,
  heraldry.nsf/request?OpenForm). Nothing here is copied from, or claims to be,
  the real internal design.

  Design summary (see acl.dxl, forms/, views/, agents/, xpages/):
    Forms   : Request (DD1348-6 header), RequestLine, SESFlagRequest, Vendor,
              HeraldicItem, Requester, Profile; subform sfRequesterPOC
    Views   : RequestsByStatus, RequestsByUnit, RequestsByDODAAC, OpenVendorWork,
              StatusInquiry, SESFlagQueue, HeraldicCatalog, Vendors, ($All), ($Lookups)
    Agents  : ReleaseToVendor (manual), CancelRequest (manual), SendStatusMail
              (scheduled hourly), RebuildStatusInquiryIndex (scheduled nightly)
    XPages  : HeraldryHome, Request, ModifyRequest, StatusInquiry, SESFlag,
              VendorQueue, Login; custom controls ccLayout, ccStatusBanner
    Script  : HAASCommon, HAASValidation, HAASMail (LotusScript);
              HAASStatus.jss, HAASRequest.jss (SSJS)

  Template inheritance: none (design was detached from the "HeraldryV2"
  template in 2013 when the classic forms were re-skinned with XPages).
  Full-text index: enabled, updated daily (see notes.ini.sample UPDATE_FULLTEXT_THREAD).
  The public-facing pages historically lived in heraldryhome.nsf; in HAAS they
  are consolidated into heraldry.nsf and the harness aliases /heraldryhome.nsf/.
-->
